      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Cooked poultry should ideally be consumed or reheated within 3 to 4 days if stored at or below 41°F (5°C), though some guidelines extend this to 7 days if daily temperature checks are strictly maintained. Do not leave the food out for more than 24 hours before refrigeration to minimize the risk of bacterial proliferation. While *Clostridium perfringens* is not always visible or detectable by sight or smell in early stages, you should ensure the meat looks moist rather than dry, smells fresh without a sulfide or sour odor, and has a uniform texture to rule out spoilage or early contamination. Always reheat leftovers to an internal temperature of 165°F (74°C) before serving to ensure safety.",
