      "content": "Common hidden contamination risks often stem from cross-contact with unclean surfaces, utensils, or hands between raw meats and cooked poultry during prep. Staff might also fail to clean splash zones around sinks or mist kitchens, allowing pathogens to settle on food covers or equipment before serving. Additionally, crowded workstations can lead to \"touch contamination\" where everyone handles the tray before it hits plating, bypassing your time-temperature controls. To mitigate this, implement strict color-coding systems for cutlery and pans, and require a dedicated \"cooking zone\" that is always kept clear of unclean items.",
